description:
The pipeline of a custom OpenSearch analyzer: char filters that clean the raw text, a tokenizer that splits it into tokens, and a chain of token filters that transform those tokens. Direct parallel to an OpenSearch <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/custom-analyzer/'>custom analyzer</a>; refer to that page for what each piece does and to the inventories of available <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/character-filters/index/'>char filters</a>, <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/tokenizers/index/'>tokenizers</a>, and <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/token-filters/index/'>token filters</a> for the exhaustive list of names and parameters. A minimal example (standard tokenizer with lowercase folding):

  {
    "tokenizer": { "name": "standard" },
    "indexFilterOrder":  ["lowercase"],
    "searchFilterOrder": ["lowercase"]
  }

A stemming example (English stop words + Porter stem) — note 'lowercase' comes before stop and stemmer so the English stop list and stemmer see lowercase input:

  {
    "tokenizer": { "name": "standard" },
    "tokenFilters": [
      { "name": "english_stop",    "definition": "{\"type\":\"stop\",\"stopwords\":\"_english_\"}" },
      { "name": "english_stemmer", "definition": "{\"type\":\"stemmer\",\"language\":\"english\"}" }
    ],
    "indexFilterOrder":  ["lowercase", "english_stop", "english_stemmer"],
    "searchFilterOrder": ["lowercase", "english_stop", "english_stemmer"]
  }

An autocomplete example (edge n-gram at index, plain match at search) — the asymmetric pattern:

  {
    "tokenizer": { "name": "standard" },
    "tokenFilters": [
      { "name": "autocomplete_ngram", "definition": "{\"type\":\"edge_ngram\",\"min_gram\":2,\"max_gram\":20}" }
    ],
    "indexFilterOrder":  ["lowercase", "autocomplete_ngram"],
    "searchFilterOrder": ["lowercase"]
  }

A synonym example — declare WHERE synonyms go in the chain using the reserved 'synapse_synonyms' token; the SynonymSets listed on the SearchConfiguration are then expanded in place:

  {
    "tokenizer": { "name": "standard" },
    "indexFilterOrder":  ["lowercase", "synapse_synonyms"],
    "searchFilterOrder": ["lowercase", "synapse_synonyms"]
  }
